  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>aprepitant</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>A04AD12</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Nijstad AL et al. 2023</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>pediatric patients</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>aprepitant</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_aprepitant/Aprepitant_Nijstad2023_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>CL 70kg (L/h)</td><td>5.83</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>V 70kg (L)</td><td>86.8</td><td>L</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>MAT (h)</td><td>1.78</td><td>h</td><td><small>MAT</small></td></tr><tr><td>F1 (%)</td><td>83</td><td></td><td><small>Fab</small></td></tr></table><h4>About aprepitant</h4><p>Aprepitant is an antiemetic (an NK1 receptor antagonist) used to prevent nausea and vomiting, including chemotherapy-induced and postoperative nausea and vomiting. It is authorised in the European Union and is widely used, mainly in cancer care to help control vomiting caused by treatment.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q621834\">Wikidata Q621834</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Aprepitant\">Aprepitant</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Nijstad AL et al. (2023). A simple extemporaneous oral suspension of aprepitant yields sufficient pharmacokinetic exposure in children. <i>Journal of oncology pharmacy practice : official publication of the International Society of Oncology Pharmacy Practitioners 29(4):899–904</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1177/10781552221089243\">10.1177/10781552221089243</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35377726\">35377726</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Nijstad_2023: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
